<td id="S5.T4.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:12.0pt;padding-right:12.0pt;">0.46</td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Black-box evaluation of <span id="S5.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DR-IKE</span> against the in-context editing baseline (<span id="S5.T4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">IKE</span>) using the <a href="https://www.kaggle.com/models/google/gemini-2.0-flash-api/Api/gemini-2.0-flash/1" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Gemini-2.0-Flash API on Kaggle</a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7 </span>Extended Evaluation on Benchmark Datasets</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further evaluated <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DR-IKE</span> on two additional benchmarks: zsRE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Meng et al. (2023b)</a></cite> and WikiDataCounterFact <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhong et al. (2023)</a></cite>. Both datasets include a broader range of edit types and formats. The same experimental setup as in the main paper was used, with the <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaMA-3.1-8B</span> model. Notably, the average similarity to <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-nearest neighbors is substantially lower in zsRE (0.4042) and WikiDataCF (0.4507) than in CounterFact (0.5695), indicating that these datasets contain more diverse and less redundant examples. This demonstrates that <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DR-IKE</span> maintains strong performance even in lower-similarity, low-resource settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.7 Extended Evaluation on Benchmark Datasets ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Dynamic Retriever for In-Context Knowledge Editing via Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <span id="S5.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DR-IKE</span> achieves consistently higher Edit Success Rate (ESR) and Paraphrase Consistency (PC) compared to the in-context editing baseline (<span id="S5.SS7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">IKE</span>). Retain Rate (RR) is also reported alongside ESR and PC, providing a more complete picture of the trade-off between successful edits, generalization, and preservation of unrelated knowledge.</p>
</div>
