<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix: Training Procedure for the Dynamic Retriever</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Training Protocol for Dynamic Example Selection</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          initial parameters <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>;  training set <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>; 
max shots <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>;  learning rate <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          trained retriever <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and budget threshold <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">epoch</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{epochs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>epochs</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{epochs}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">each</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,\,y_{\text{new}})\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,\,y_{\text{new}})\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Fixed <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Copy</span> / <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Update</span> demos for <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> candidates

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
               (pre-selected via embeddings)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leftarrow S_{\theta}(x,\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leftarrow S_{\theta}(x,\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> scalar scores
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leftarrow\mathrm{softmax}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leftarrow\mathrm{softmax}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> policy distribution
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow\min\!\bigl(K,\,|\{i\mid p_{i}&gt;\sigma\}|\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow\min\!\bigl(K,\,|\{i\mid p_{i}&gt;\sigma\}|\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textit{prev}\_r\leftarrow\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">prev</mtext><mi>_</mi><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{prev}\_r\leftarrow\bot</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{j}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{j}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> top-<math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retains</span> from <math id="alg1.l17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="alg1.l17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
               Prompt with <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Copy</span>, <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Update</span>, <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
               query LLM <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow\begin{cases}+1,&amp;\hat{y}=y_{\text{new}}\\
-1,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow\begin{cases}+1,&amp;\hat{y}=y_{\text{new}}\\
-1,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leftarrow(j&gt;1)\wedge(\textit{prev\_r}=+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">prev_r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leftarrow(j&gt;1)\wedge(\textit{prev\_r}=+1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
                 <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\wedge(r=-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\wedge(r=-1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
               <span id="alg1.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
            
            
                <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\leftarrow\max\!\bigl(\sigma,\;\max_{i&gt;j}p_{i}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\leftarrow\max\!\bigl(\sigma,\;\max_{i&gt;j}p_{i}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
            
            
               <span id="alg1.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\mathrel{+}=-\,r\;\log p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">+</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.447em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\mathrel{+}=-\,r\;\log p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
            
            
               <span id="alg1.l27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prev</span>_r <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow r</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta-\alpha\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta-\alpha\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l29.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> REINFORCE
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">30:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">31:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The overall training protocol for our dynamic retriever is illustrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix A Appendix: Training Procedure for the Dynamic Retriever ‣ Dynamic Retriever for In-Context Knowledge Editing via Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. At the beginning of each epoch, we initialize the retriever’s parameters <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and the budget threshold <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. For every training instance <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y_{\mathrm{new}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y_{\mathrm{new}})</annotation></semantics></math> in the dataset, we first construct the fixed <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Copy</span> and <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Update</span> demonstrations based on semantic similarity using embeddings from a 20M-parameter Sentence Transformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reimers and Gurevych (2020)</a></cite>. These fixed components serve as the foundational part of every in-context prompt. Next, we select a candidate pool <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> of <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples—again using the same embedding space—to identify potentially helpful facts related to the input.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Once the <span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> pool is constructed, the retriever’s scoring function <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates each candidate, producing scalar relevance scores which are normalized via softmax to obtain a probability distribution <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> over the pool. The retriever then determines how many examples to select, based on the current value of <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, by choosing the top candidates whose probabilities exceed the threshold. If none of the probabilities surpass <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, we ensure that at least one <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> is selected to prevent empty prompt construction. This mechanism enables the retriever to modulate prompt length dynamically, balancing retrieval confidence with context limitations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We then proceed to construct the full in-context prompt incrementally by adding one <span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> example at a time (top-<math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>). After each addition, we query the language model and check if its output matches the desired edited response <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A binary reward <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{+1,-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{+1,-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is assigned depending on whether the answer is correct. If adding a particular <span id="A1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> causes a correct prediction to flip to incorrect, we treat it as a degradation in prompt quality and increase the threshold <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> to exclude lower-probability examples in future steps. This allows the model to prune less useful <span id="A1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retains</span> early and adapt the prompt construction strategy over time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout the episode, we accumulate REINFORCE-style loss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams (1992)</a></cite> using the reward signal and the log-probability of each selected <span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span>. The resulting gradient is used to update only the retriever’s scoring head via policy gradient. By repeating this process across training epochs, the retriever learns not just which <span id="A1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples are most helpful for factual editing, but also how to dynamically adjust its selection budget to optimize both model performance and context efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix: Retain Budget Distribution Across Models</h2>

<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.21059v1/images/llama_budget.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/250;" width="381" height="250" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="A2.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> budget distribution for LLaMA 3.1-8B under DR-IKE. Each bar shows the frequency of a given <span id="A2.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> count per prompt. Mean = <math id="A2.F5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{3.02}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">3.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{3.02}</annotation></semantics></math>, Std = <math id="A2.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0.96}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.96</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0.96}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.21059v1/images/qwen_budget.png" id="A2.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/252;" width="381" height="252" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A2.F5.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> budget distribution for Qwen 2.5-7B under DR-IKE. The model allocates more <span id="A2.F5.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples for edits requiring stronger contextual support. Mean = <math id="A2.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{3.72}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">3.72</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{3.72}</annotation></semantics></math>, Std = <math id="A2.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1.15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">1.15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1.15}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed framework, <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DR-IKE</span>, dynamically selects the number of <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples per prompt based on their estimated contribution to edit success, rather than applying a fixed number across all edits. Fig. <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Retain Budget Distribution Across Models ‣ Dynamic Retriever for In-Context Knowledge Editing via Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix B Appendix: Retain Budget Distribution Across Models ‣ Dynamic Retriever for In-Context Knowledge Editing via Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> illustrate how the number of <span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples varies per edit instance for two different LLMs. In contrast to IKE, which statically includes 16 <span id="A2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retains</span> regardless of their informativeness or utility, DR-IKE tailors the prompt length to the needs of each specific edit.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This adaptivity yields significant efficiency gains. On average, LLaMA 3.1-8B requires only <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{3.02\pm 0.96}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">3.02</mn><mo>±</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">0.96</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{3.02\pm 0.96}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Retain</span> examples per prompt, while Qwen 2.5-7B uses <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{3.72\pm 1.15}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">3.72</mn><mo>±</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">1.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{3.72\pm 1.15}</annotation></semantics></math>. These compact prompts reduce both the computational overhead and the risk of introducing irrelevant or distracting context. Notably, despite using fewer examples, DR-IKE maintains competitive or even superior edit success compared to IKE. This highlights the importance of selective inclusion: by pruning redundant or low-impact examples, DR-IKE not only saves prompt space but also enhances factual precision and generalization. The results underscore the utility of adaptive demonstration selection as a scalable solution for black-box knowledge editing.</p>
</div>
</section>
